# can0 -- the DIAG bus (external diagnostic / contestant side).
#
# ROLE NAMES, NOT NUMBERS. The drive bus is the HIGHER-numbered interface here,
# which is the opposite of what most people assume and the opposite of the original
# design doc. Verified on hardware 2026-08-01: the motors and BMS answer on can1;
# can0 has no nodes and writes fail with ENOBUFS (no ACK). Trust the car, not the doc.
#
# Nothing is permanently attached to this bus -- it terminates at the side tap, a
# snap connector on an extension run from the Pi. It is SILENT by design until a
# contestant plugs in a CAN FD adapter, and transmits fail with ENOBUFS until they
# do, because a lone node gets no acknowledgement. That is correct and authentic
# behaviour for a diagnostic port, not a fault.
#
# CAN FD: 500 kbit/s arbitration, 1 Mbit/s data. FD is what lets the UDS server
# return a flag inside a single 64-byte response with no ISO-TP multi-frame
# anywhere. FDMode=/DataBitRate= in [CAN] need systemd >= 246; scarthgap ships 255.
[Match]
Name=can0

[CAN]
BitRate=500000
DataBitRate=1000000
FDMode=yes
